---
const PIN_SIDES = ["top", "right", "bottom", "left"];
const PINS_PER_SIDE = 15;

const traces = [
  { d: "M 33.5 29 L 33.5 9 L 14 9", gold: true },
  { d: "M 50 29 L 50 0", gold: true },
  { d: "M 66.5 29 L 66.5 15 L 88 15", endpoint: [88, 15] },
  { d: "M 71 43 L 99 43", gold: true },
  { d: "M 71 60 L 92 60 L 92 80", endpoint: [92, 80] },
  { d: "M 62 71 L 62 94 L 82 94", gold: true },
  { d: "M 38 71 L 38 96", endpoint: [38, 96] },
  { d: "M 29 60 L 6 60 L 6 80", gold: true },
  { d: "M 40 34 L 1 34", endpoint: [1, 34] },
];

const nodes = [
  {
    id: "workload",
    title: "Processor Workload",
    position: "top: 4%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);",
    short: "How the AGC handled many tasks with limited computing resources.",
    content: `The AGC used a real-time operating system called <code>EXECUTIVE</code> to manage software jobs. Every scheduled job required <strong>one of only eight core sets</strong>, each containing <strong>12 erasable memory registers</strong> that stored the job's execution state. This allowed interrupted jobs to resume later. As more jobs competed for these limited resources, the processor had to manage more work simultaneously, increasing its overall processor workload.`,
    takeaway:
      "The AGC continuously managed competing jobs using a small pool of processing resources. Even under heavy demand during the lunar descent, the workload management allowed the computer to support a successful landing.",
  },
  {
    id: "priority",
    title: "Task Prioritization",
    position: "top: 9%; left: 14%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);",
    short: "How the AGC decided which jobs should run first.",
    content: `The AGC used a <strong>preemptive priority-based scheduling algorithm</strong>. Every job was assigned a priority level, allowing higher-priority jobs to interrupt lower-priority ones when necessary. Jobs requiring additional temporary storage could also request one of <strong> five Vector Accumulator (VAC) areas</strong>. During processor overload, lower-priority jobs could be delayed or discarded so <strong> critical flight operations</strong> could continue.`,
    takeaway:
      "Priority scheduling ensured that critical flight operations always executed first. This ensured that the most essential operations continued even when processor resources became limited.",
  },
  {
    id: "realtime",
    title: "Real-Time Operation",
    position: "top: 85%; left: 6%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);",
    short: "Why correct timing was as important as correct computation.",
    content: `The AGC was a <strong>strict real-time system</strong>, meaning certain jobs had to execute at <strong>exact times</strong>. Its <code>WAITLIST</code> program scheduled <strong>time-critical jobs</strong> such as processing sensor data and triggering spacecraft events. Because the processor executes instructions sequentially, real-time scheduling ensured time-critical instructions—like engine throttle adjustments and navigation updates—were completed strictly before their deadlines.`,
    takeaway:
      "Executing critical jobs at the correct time was essential for accurate guidance and control. Missing a guidance loop cycle would result in inaccurate navigation and potential mission failure.",
  },
  {
    id: "alarm",
    title: "Memory Constraints",
    position: "top: 42%; left: 96%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);",
    short:
      "What the program alarms actually meant during the Apollo 11 landing.",
    content: `The <code>1201</code> and <code>1202</code> alarms were not signs of hardware failure, but warnings of memory constraints. An <strong>Executive Overflow</strong> meant the operating system had exhausted its scheduling resources. A <code>1202</code> alarm meant <strong>no core sets were available</strong>, while a <code>1201</code> alarm meant <strong>no Vector Accumulator (VAC) areas remained</strong> for temporary storage. These alarms indicated that the computer had reached its resource limits while trying to manage unnecessary radar processing requests.`,
    takeaway:
      "The alarms warned that scheduling resources were exhausted, not that the computer had crashed. Rather than signaling mission failure, the alarms actually demonstrated that the computer was working as intended, still successfully managing resources to protect critical flight operations.",
  },
  {
    id: "recovery",
    title: "Fault Recovery",
    position: "top: 94%; left: 82%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);",
    short: "How the AGC continued operating during overload.",
    content: `The AGC was designed for fault recovery from overloads instead of shutting down. When the <code>EXECUTIVE</code> could no longer allocate scheduling resources, it invoked the <code>BAILOUT1</code> recovery routine. The system performed a <strong>software restart</strong>, discarded unnecessary <strong>low-priority jobs</strong>, and restarted essential guidance and control programs near where they had been interrupted.`,
    takeaway:
      "Automatic recovery allowed the AGC to continue operating without interrupting its critical flight functions. Since essential flight data and high-priority tasks were preserved, the Lunar Module remained under control even with the repeated executive overflows, which ultimately led to a successful landing.",
  },
];
---

<section id="architecture">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-kicker">Apollo 11 / Architecture</p>

    <h1 class="section-heading">Computer Architecture Concept</h1>

    <p class="section-description">
      The Apollo Guidance Computer (AGC) guided and controlled the Apollo 11
      Lunar Module Eagle during its descent to the Moon. Using only a 2.048 MHz
      processor, 4 KB of RAM, and 72 KB of ROM, its software architecture
      enabled reliable real-time operation despite the severe hardware
      limitations of the 1960s.
      <strong
        >To explore the AGC's architecture, click any of the <span
          class="text-gold">yellow nodes</span
        >.</strong
      >
    </p>

    <div class="architecture-layout">
      <div class="chip-container">
        <svg class="chip-traces" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true">
          {
            traces.map((trace) => (
              <g>
                <path
                  d={trace.d}
                  class={`chip-trace-path ${trace.gold ? "gold" : ""}`}
                />
                {trace.endpoint && (
                  <circle
                    cx={trace.endpoint[0]}
                    cy={trace.endpoint[1]}
                    r="4.5"
                    class="chip-trace-node"
                  />
                )}
              </g>
            ))
          }
        </svg>

        <h1 class="chip">AGC</h1>

        {
          nodes.map((node) => (
            <button
              class="chip-node hinted"
              style={node.position}
              data-node-id={node.id}
              aria-label={node.title}
            />
          ))
        }

        {
          PIN_SIDES.map((side) => (
            <div class={`chip-pins chip-pins-${side}`} aria-hidden="true">
              {Array.from({ length: PINS_PER_SIDE }, () => (
                <span class="chip-pin" />
              ))}
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <div class="info-overlay" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="info-panel">
          <div class="info-panel-content" id="info-panel-empty">
            <div class="info-panel-empty">
              <p class="info-panel-hint">
                Select a yellow node to learn more about Apollo 11's AGC
                architecture!
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          {
            nodes.map((node) => (
              <div
                class="info-panel-content hidden"
                id={`info-panel-${node.id}`}
              >
                <h3>{node.title}</h3>
                <p class="info-panel-short">{node.short}</p>
                <p set:html={node.content} />
                <div class="takeaway">
                  <h4>Key Takeaway & Relevance to the Mission</h4>
                  <p>{node.takeaway}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="architecture-footer">
      <p>
        Explore the Apollo Guidance Computer's program code used during the
        Apollo 11 mission through the
        <a
          href="https://github.com/virtualagc/virtualagc/tree/master/Luminary099"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Luminary099 source code
        </a> available on the Virtual AGC repository on GitHub.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(".chip-node");
  const panels = document.querySelectorAll(".info-panel-content") as NodeListOf<HTMLElement>;
  const emptyPanel = document.getElementById("info-panel-empty");
  const overlay = document.querySelector(".info-overlay") as HTMLElement | null;
  const infoPanel = document.querySelector(".info-panel");

  let selectedId: string | null = null;

  function selectNode(id: string | null) {
    if (selectedId === id) {
      id = null;
    }
    selectedId = id;

    buttons.forEach((btn) => {
      const btnId = btn.getAttribute("data-node-id");
      if (btnId === id) {
        btn.classList.add("active");
        btn.classList.remove("hinted");
      } else {
        btn.classList.remove("active");
        btn.classList.add("hinted");
      }
    });

    if (overlay) {
      if (id) {
        overlay.classList.add("is-open");
        overlay.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "false");
      } else {
        overlay.classList.remove("is-open");
        overlay.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");
      }
    }

    panels.forEach((panel) => {
      panel.classList.add("hidden");
      panel.style.animation = "none";
    });

    if (overlay) void overlay.offsetWidth;

    if (id) {
      const activePanel = document.getElementById(`info-panel-${id}`);
      if (activePanel) {
        activePanel.classList.remove("hidden");
        activePanel.style.animation = "";
      }
    } else {
      if (emptyPanel) {
        emptyPanel.classList.remove("hidden");
        emptyPanel.style.animation = "";
      }
    }
  }

  buttons.forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
      e.stopPropagation();
      selectNode(btn.getAttribute("data-node-id"));
    });
  });

  if (overlay) overlay.addEventListener("click", () => selectNode(null));
  if (infoPanel)
    infoPanel.addEventListener("click", (e) => e.stopPropagation());
</script>

<style>
  .architecture-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(250px, 0.34fr) minmax(390px, 0.66fr);
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 4rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    min-height: 500px;
  }

  /* ---------- CHIP CONTAINER ---------- */

  .chip-container {
    position: relative;
    width: min(100%, 340px);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    margin: auto;
    isolation: isolate;
    --chip-body-size: 146px;
    --chip-pin-gap: 10px;
  }

  /* ---------- PINS ----------
   No per-pin coordinates: each side is a flex row/column that
   distributes its own children evenly along the chip edge. */

  .chip-pins {
    position: absolute;
    display: flex;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .chip-pins-top,
  .chip-pins-bottom {
    left: 50%;
    width: calc(var(--chip-body-size) - 30px);
    justify-content: space-between;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }

  .chip-pins-top {
    top: calc(50% - (var(--chip-body-size) / 2) - var(--chip-pin-gap));
  }

  .chip-pins-bottom {
    bottom: calc(50% - (var(--chip-body-size) / 2) - var(--chip-pin-gap));
  }

  .chip-pins-left,
  .chip-pins-right {
    top: 50%;
    height: calc(var(--chip-body-size) - 30px);
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }

  .chip-pins-left {
    left: calc(50% - (var(--chip-body-size) / 2) - var(--chip-pin-gap));
  }

  .chip-pins-right {
    right: calc(50% - (var(--chip-body-size) / 2) - var(--chip-pin-gap));
  }

  .chip-pin {
    background: var(--primary-light);
    opacity: 0.85;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.2);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .chip-pins-top .chip-pin,
  .chip-pins-bottom .chip-pin {
    width: 5px;
    height: 16px;
  }

  .chip-pins-left .chip-pin,
  .chip-pins-right .chip-pin {
    width: 16px;
    height: 5px;
  }

  /* ---------- CIRCUIT TRACES ----------
   One SVG layer for every line + node instead of matched pairs
   of absolutely-positioned divs. Coordinates live in one <path>
   per trace, so a line and its endpoint can never drift apart. */

  .chip-traces {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .chip-trace-path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--primary-light);
    stroke-width: 0.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .chip-trace-path.gold {
    stroke: var(--amber);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .chip-trace-node {
    fill: var(--primary-light);
    stroke: #1a1430;
    stroke-width: 0.6;
  }

  /* ---------- CHIP BODY ---------- */

  .chip {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);

    width: 146px;
    height: 146px;

    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;

    border: 2px solid var(--primary-light);
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 50% 35%,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16),
        transparent 42%
      ),
      linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(87, 38, 186), rgba(39, 16, 95));

    border-radius: 18px;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08) inset,
      0 18px 45px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.32),
      0 0 26px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.12);

    z-index: 3;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .chip::before,
  .chip::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: -15px;
    border-radius: 22px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* ---------- INTERACTIVE NODES ---------- */

  .chip-node {
    position: absolute;
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, var(--gold), var(--amber));
    border: 3px solid #1a1430;
    border-radius: 50%;
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 12;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 6px rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.05),
      0 0 14px rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.18);
    transition:
      scale 300ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),
      box-shadow 300ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),
      background 300ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),
      border-color 300ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),
      filter 300ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .chip-node.hinted {
    animation: pulseGlow 2.2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .chip-node:hover {
      scale: 1.15;
    }

    .chip-node.hinted:hover {
      animation: none;
      scale: 1.15;
      filter: brightness(1.4) contrast(1.2);
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 8px rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.4),
        0 0 35px rgba(255, 250, 160, 0.95),
        0 0 55px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.5);
    }
  }

  .chip-node::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: -8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.22);
  }

  .chip-node::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    background: rgba(26, 20, 48, 0.7);
  }

  .chip-node.active {
    scale: 1.2;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 18px rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.8),
      0 0 0 8px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4),
      0 0 24px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.4);
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #fffcf0, var(--gold));
    border-color: #ffffff;
    z-index: 15;
  }

  @keyframes pulseGlow {
    0%,
    100% {
      filter: brightness(1.4) contrast(1.2);
      scale: 1.15;
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 8px rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.4),
        0 0 35px rgba(255, 250, 160, 0.95),
        0 0 55px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.5);
    }
    50% {
      filter: brightness(1);
      scale: 1;
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 6px rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.12),
        0 0 22px rgba(255, 224, 110, 0.72),
        0 0 38px rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.22);
    }
  }

  /* ---------- INFO PANEL ---------- */

  .info-panel {
    height: 460px;
    padding: 2rem 1rem 2rem 2rem;
    border: 1px solid
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary-light) 18%, var(--border));
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at top right,
        rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.12),
        transparent 35%
      ),
      linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03),
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.01)
      );
    border-radius: 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .info-panel-empty {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .info-panel-short {
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--primary-light);
  }

  .info-panel-hint {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .info-panel h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .takeaway {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber);
    background: rgba(245, 192, 0, 0.05);
    border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
  }

  .info-overlay {
    display: contents;
  }

  .info-panel-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    animation: panelFadeIn 400ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1) forwards;

    flex: 1;
    overflow-y: auto;
    padding-right: 1rem;
    scrollbar-width: thin;
    scrollbar-color: var(--amber) transparent;
  }

  .info-panel-content::before,
  .info-panel-content::after {
    content: "";
    margin: auto;
  }

  .info-panel-content::-webkit-scrollbar {
    width: 6px;
  }

  .info-panel-content::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
    background: transparent;
  }

  .info-panel-content::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
    background: var(--gold);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .hidden {
    display: none !important;
  }

  @keyframes panelFadeIn {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(8px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .architecture-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
      justify-items: center;
    }

    .chip-container {
      width: min(100%, 300px);
    }

    .chip-node {
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
    }

    .chip-node::before {
      inset: -4px;
    }

    .info-overlay {
      display: contents;
    }

    .info-panel {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      min-height: 460px;
      max-height: none;
      overflow: visible;
      margin: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
